{"content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Why Is the Sky Blue? 天空为什么是蓝色的？</title>
<style>
  *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
  :root{
    --bg:#0b1020;--card:#111827;--text:#e2e8f0;--text-dim:#94a3b8;
    --accent:#38bdf8;--accent2:#818cf8;--border:#1e293b;
    --toddler:#34d399;--teen:#fbbf24;--phd:#f472b6;
  }
  html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
  body{
    font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,"Helvetica Neue",Arial,"Noto Sans SC","PingFang SC","Microsoft YaHei",sans-serif;
    background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;
    min-height:100vh;
  }

  /* Header */
  header{
    text-align:center;padding:2.5rem 1rem 1.5rem;
    background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0b1020 0%,#1a1a3e 100%);
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  }
  header h1{font-size:1.8rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.3rem}
  header h1 .en{color:var(--accent)}
  header h1 .zh{color:var(--accent2);font-size:1.3rem}
  header p{color:var(--text-dim);font-size:.9rem;margin-top:.4rem}

  /* Level selector */
  .controls{
    display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:.6rem;
    padding:1rem 1rem .5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;
  }
  .controls button{
    padding:.5rem 1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius:999px;background:var(--card);color:var(--text-dim);
    cursor:pointer;font-size:.85rem;transition:all .2s;
  }
  .controls button:hover{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent)}
  .controls button.active{
    background:var(--accent);color:#000;border-color:var(--accent);
    font-weight:600;
  }

  /* Main content */
  main{max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:1rem}

  .slide{display:none}
  .slide.active{display:block}

  /* Bilingual layout */
  .bilingual{
    display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0;
    background:var(--card);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;
    border:1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .bilingual .col{
    padding:1.8rem 2rem;position:relative;
  }
  .bilingual .col:first-child{border-right:1px solid var(--border)}

  .col-label{
    display:inline-block;font-size:.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.1em;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:1rem;
    padding:.2rem .6rem;border-radius:4px;
  }
  .col-label.en{background:rgba(56,189,248,.12);color:var(--accent)}
  .col-label.zh{background:rgba(129,140,248,.12);color:var(--accent2)}

  .col h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.4}
  .col h3{font-size:1.05rem;margin:1.2rem 0 .6rem;color:var(--text)}
  .col p,.col li{font-size:.92rem;color:var(--text-dim);margin-bottom:.6rem}
  .col ol,.col ul{padding-left:1.4rem;margin-bottom:.8rem}
  .col li{margin-bottom:.3rem}

  .col .highlight{color:var(--text);font-weight:500}

  /* Math block */
  .math-block{
    background:#0f172a;border:1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius:8px;padding:1rem 1.2rem;margin:.8rem 0;
    overflow-x:auto;text-align:center;
  }
  .math-block .eq{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--text);display:inline-block}

  /* Level badges */
  .badge{
    display:inline-block;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:600;
    padding:.25rem .7rem;border-radius:999px;margin-bottom:.8rem;
  }
  .badge.toddler{background:rgba(52,211,153,.12);color:var(--toddler);border:1px solid rgba(52,211,153,.25)}
  .badge.teen{background:rgba(251,191,36,.12);color:var(--teen);border:1px solid rgba(251,191,36,.25)}
  .badge.phd{background:rgba(244,114,182,.12);color:var(--phd);border:1px solid rgba(244,114,182,.25)}

  /* Footer */
  footer{
    text-align:center;padding:2rem 1rem;
    color:var(--text-dim);font-size:.75rem;
    border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin-top:2rem;
  }

  /* Nav dots */
  .dots{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:.5rem;padding:.8rem 0}
  .dot{
    width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;
    background:var(--border);cursor:pointer;transition:all .2s;
  }
  .dot.active{background:var(--accent);transform:scale(1.25)}

  /* Keyboard nav hint */
  .nav-hint{
    text-align:center;color:var(--text-dim);font-size:.72rem;
    padding-bottom:.5rem;
  }
  .nav-hint kbd{
    background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius:3px;padding:.1rem .4rem;font-size:.7rem;
    margin:0 .15rem;
  }

  @media(max-width:768px){
    .bilingual{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .bilingual .col:first-child{border-right:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
    header h1{font-size:1.4rem}
    header h1 .zh{font-size:1.1rem}
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <h1><span class="en">Why Is the Sky Blue?</span> <span class="zh">天空为什么是蓝色的？</span></h1>
  <p>A bilingual explanation at three levels &nbsp;|&nbsp; 三种水平的双语解释</p>
</header>

<nav class="controls" id="controls">
  <button data-slide="0" class="active">👶 Toddler 幼儿</button>
  <button data-slide="1">🎒 Teen 高中生</button>
  <button data-slide="2">🔬 PhD 博士</button>
</nav>

<div class="nav-hint">
  <kbd>←</kbd> <kbd>→</kbd> arrow keys &nbsp; or &nbsp; click a level
</div>

<main id="main">

  <!-- ===================== SLIDE 0: TODDLER ===================== -->
  <div class="slide active" data-index="0">
    <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:.8rem">
      <span class="badge toddler">Level 1 · 第一级</span>
    </div>
    <div class="bilingual">
      <div class="col">
        <span class="col-label en">English</span>
        <h2>👶 For a 3-Year-Old</h2>
        <p>Did you know that sunlight looks white, but it's actually made of <span class="highlight">*all* the colors of the rainbow</span> — red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet!</p>
        <p>When sunlight comes down to Earth, it bumps into tiny bits of air in the sky. The <span class="highlight">blue color is really little and bouncy</span>, so it zooms all around the sky and bounces around everywhere! That's why when you look up, you see lots and lots of blue — the blue light has bounced all over for you to see!</p>
        <p>Red and orange light are big and lazy, so they just go straight through the air without bouncing around. That's why the sky looks blue, but at sunset, the red light gets to show off and paints the sky in pretty orange and red colors!</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <span class="col-label zh">简体中文</span>
        <h2>👶 讲给三岁小朋友听</h2>
        <p>你知道吗？阳光看起来是白色的，但它其实是由<span class="highlight">彩虹里所有的颜色</span>组成的——红、橙、黄、绿、蓝、靛、紫！</p>
        <p>当阳光到达地球时，它会碰到天空中的微小空气微粒。<span class="highlight">蓝色光非常小又很活泼</span>，所以它会在天空中到处乱窜、到处乱跳！这就是为什么当你抬头看天空时，你会看到很多很多蓝色——蓝色光已经为你跳遍了整个天空！</p>
        <p>红色和橙色光又大又懒，所以它们就直接穿过空气，到处乱跳。这就是为什么天空看起来是蓝色的，但在日落时，红色光就会出来展示自己，把天空染成漂亮的橙色和红色！</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ===================== SLIDE 1: HIGH SCHOOL ===================== -->
  <div class="slide" data-index="1">
    <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:.8rem">
      <span class="badge teen">Level 2 · 第二级</span>
    </div>
    <div class="bilingual">
      <div class="col">
        <span class="col-label en">English</span>
        <h2>🎒 For a High School Student</h2>
        <p>The sky is blue because of something called <span class="highlight">Rayleigh scattering</span> — named after the British physicist Lord Rayleigh who figured it out in the 1800s.</p>
        <p>Here's how it works:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><span class="highlight">Sunlight looks white but isn't</span> — it's a mixture of all visible wavelengths, from red (longer wavelengths, ~700 nm) to violet/blue (shorter wavelengths, ~400 nm).</li>
          <li><span class="highlight">The atmosphere is full of gas molecules</span> — mostly nitrogen and oxygen, which are incredibly tiny compared to the wavelength of visible light.</li>
          <li><span class="highlight">Shorter wavelengths scatter more</span> — when light hits these molecules, it scatters in all directions. The amount of scattering is <em>inversely proportional to the fourth power of the wavelength</em> (∝ 1/λ⁴). This means blue and violet light scatter about 10× more than red light.</li>
          <li><span class="highlight">Our eyes prefer blue over violet</span> — technically, violet light scatters *even more* than blue light. But our sun emits more blue light than violet light, and our eyes are simply much more sensitive to blue. So we perceive the scattered light as blue, not violet.</li>
        </ol>
        <h3>Why is sunset red?</h3>
        <p>At sunset, sunlight has to travel through <em>way more</em> atmosphere to reach your eyes. By the time it gets here, almost all the blue and green light has been scattered away, leaving behind the longer-wavelength reds, oranges, and yellows — which is why sunsets look so dramatic!</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <span class="col-label zh">简体中文</span>
        <h2>🎒 讲给高中生听</h2>
        <p>天空之所以是蓝色的，是因为一个叫<span class="highlight">瑞利散射</span>的现象——以在19世纪发现这一现象的英国物理学家瑞利勋爵命名。</p>
        <p>它是这样工作的：</p>
        <ol>
          <li><span class="highlight">阳光看起来是白色的，但其实不是</span>——它是所有可见波长的混合体，从红色（较长波长，约700纳米）到紫色/蓝色（较短波长，约400纳米）。</li>
          <li><span class="highlight">大气层中充满了气体分子</span>——主要是氮气和氧气，它们的尺寸相对于可见光的波长来说极其微小。</li>
          <li><span class="highlight">波长越短，散射越多</span>——当光撞到这些分子时，它会在各个方向上散射。散射的量<em>与波长的四次方成反比</em>（∝ 1/λ⁴）。这意味着蓝色和紫色光的散射量比红色光大约多10倍。</li>
          <li><span class="highlight">我们的眼睛更喜欢蓝色而不是紫色</span>——严格来说，紫色光的散射甚至比蓝色光更多。但太阳发出的蓝光比紫光多，而且我们的眼睛对蓝色的敏感度要高得多。所以我们感知到的散射光是蓝色的，而不是紫色的。</li>
        </ol>
        <h3>为什么日落是红色的？</h3>
        <p>在日落时，阳光需要穿过<em>更多</em>的大气层才能到达你的眼睛。到这时，几乎所有的蓝色和绿色光已经被散射掉了，只剩下波长较长的红色、橙色和黄色——这就是为什么日落看起来如此壮观！</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ===================== SLIDE 2: PHYSICS PHD ===================== -->
  <div class="slide" data-index="2">
    <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:.8rem">
      <span class="badge phd">Level 3 · 第三级</span>
    </div>
    <div class="bilingual">
      <div class="col">
        <span class="col-label en">English</span>
        <h2>🔬 For a Physics PhD</h2>
        <p>The blue sky is a classic manifestation of <span class="highlight">Rayleigh scattering</span>, arising from the elastic scattering of electromagnetic radiation by particles whose characteristic size <em>a</em> satisfies <em>a ≪ λ</em> (where λ is the wavelength of the incident radiation).</p>

        <h3>Microscopic Origin</h3>
        <p>An incident plane electromagnetic wave with electric field <em>E₀ eⁱ⁽ᵏ·ʳ⁻ωᵗ⁾</em> interacts with a gas molecule (typically N₂ or O₂) modelled as a bound electron system. The oscillating electric field induces a dipole moment:</p>
        <div class="math-block"><span class="eq">p⃗ = α(ω) E⃗₀</span></div>
        <p>where α(ω) is the frequency-dependent polarizability. In the visible regime, ω is far from any electronic resonance of nitrogen or oxygen, so α is approximately real and constant.</p>
        <p>The induced dipole radiates as a classical Hertzian dipole. The time-averaged power radiated per unit solid angle is:</p>
        <div class="math-block"><span class="eq">dP/dΩ = (ω⁴|α|²E₀² / 16π²c⁴ε₀²) · sin²θ</span></div>
        <p>Integrating over all solid angles gives the total scattered power:</p>
        <div class="math-block"><span class="eq">P_sc = (ω⁴|α|²E₀² / 6πc⁴ε₀²) ∝ 1/λ⁴</span></div>
        <p>This is the celebrated <strong>Rayleigh 1/λ⁴ law</strong>.</p>

        <h3>Why Not Violet?</h3>
        <p>The scattered spectral radiance follows the solar spectrum <em>I⊙(λ)</em> multiplied by the Rayleigh factor:</p>
        <div class="math-block"><span class="eq">I_sky(λ) ∝ I⊙(λ) / λ⁴</span></div>
        <p>While violet (400–440 nm) is scattered more than blue (440–490 nm), two effects shift our perceptual response toward blue:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><span class="highlight">Solar spectral irradiance</span> peaks near 500 nm and declines toward the violet, so there is intrinsically less violet flux available.</li>
          <li><span class="highlight">Human visual response</span> — the CIE color-matching functions have very low  z̄(λ) (S-cone) response near 400 nm. Integrating <em>I_sky(λ)</em> against these functions places the chromaticity near (x ≈ 0.24, y ≈ 0.33) — a blue sensation.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Beyond Simple Rayleigh Scattering</h3>
        <p>In the real atmosphere, <strong>Mie scattering</strong> from aerosols and water droplets (particle size <em>a ~ λ</em>) contributes a nearly wavelength-independent (gray) scattering component, partially whitening the sky. The full radiative transfer calculation requires numerical solutions (e.g., DISORT), accounting for multiple scattering, absorption by trace gases (O₃, NO₂), and surface albedo.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <span class="col-label zh">简体中文</span>
        <h2>🔬 讲给物理博士听</h2>
        <p>蔚蓝色的天空是<span class="highlight">瑞利散射</span>的经典体现，它源于电磁辐射被特征尺寸满足 <em>a ≪ λ</em> 的颗粒所弹性散射（其中 λ 为入射辐射的波长）。</p>

        <h3>微观起源</h3>
        <p>考虑一个入射平面电磁波，其电场为 <em>E₀ eⁱ⁽ᵏ·ʳ⁻ωᵗ⁾</em>，与一个气体分子（通常为 N₂ 或 O₂）相互作用，该分子可建模为束缚电子体系。振荡的电场在分子中诱导出一个偶极矩：</p>
        <div class="math-block"><span class="eq">p⃗ = α(ω) E⃗₀</span></div>
        <p>其中 α(ω) 是分子的频率依赖极化率。在可见光波段，ω 远离氮或氧的任何电子共振，因此 α 可近似取为实常数。</p>
        <p>诱导偶极子作为经典赫兹偶极子辐射。单位立体角内辐射的时间平均功率为：</p>
        <div class="math-block"><span class="eq">dP/dΩ = (ω⁴|α|²E₀² / 16π²c⁴ε₀²) · sin²θ</span></div>
        <p>对全空间积分得总散射功率：</p>
        <div class="math-block"><span class="eq">P_sc = (ω⁴|α|²E₀² / 6πc⁴ε₀²) ∝ 1/λ⁴</span></div>
        <p>这就是大名鼎鼎的<strong>瑞利 1/λ⁴ 定律</strong>。</p>

        <h3>为什么不是紫色？</h3>
        <p>散射光谱辐亮度遵循太阳光谱 <em>I⊙(λ)</em> 乘以瑞利因子：</p>
        <div class="math-block"><span class="eq">I_sky(λ) ∝ I⊙(λ) / λ⁴</span></div>
        <p>尽管紫色光（400–440 nm）的散射量比蓝色光（440–490 nm）更多，但有两个效应使我们的感知响应向蓝色偏移：</p>
        <ol>
          <li><span class="highlight">太阳光谱辐照度</span>在约500 nm处达到峰值，并向紫色端递减，因此可用于散射的紫色通量本身就较少。</li>
          <li><span class="highlight">人类视觉响应</span>——CIE 颜色匹配函数在 400 nm 附近具有非常低的 z̄(λ)（S锥细胞）响应。将 <em>I_sky(λ)</em> 与这些函数积分后，色品坐标位于约 (x ≈ 0.24, y ≈ 0.33) 附近——这是一种蓝色的感受。</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>超越简单瑞利散射</h3>
        <p>在实际大气中，气溶胶和水滴（颗粒尺寸 <em>a ~ λ</em>）的<strong>米氏散射</strong>贡献了一个几乎与波长无关（灰色）的散射分量，使天空部分变白。完整的辐射传输计算需要数值求解（如 DISORT），考虑多重散射、微量气体（O₃、NO₂）的吸收以及地表反照率。</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</main>

<div class="dots" id="dots">
  <div class="dot active" data-index="0"></div>
  <div class="dot" data-index="1"></div>
  <div class="dot" data-index="2"></div>
</div>

<footer>
  Why Is the Sky Blue? · 天空为什么是蓝色的？ &nbsp;|&nbsp; Bilingual presentation &nbsp;|&nbsp; 双语展示
</footer>

<script>
(function(){
  var slides = document.querySelectorAll('.slide');
  var buttons = document.querySelectorAll('#controls button');
  var dots = document.querySelectorAll('.dot');
  var current = 0;
  var total = slides.length;

  function goTo(n){
    slides[current].classList.remove('active');
    buttons[current].classList.remove('active');
    dots[current].classList.remove('active');
    current = (n + total) % total;
    slides[current].classList.add('active');
    buttons[current].classList.add('active');
    dots[current].classList.add('active');
  }

  buttons.forEach(function(b){
    b.addEventListener('click', function(){ goTo(parseInt(this.dataset.slide)); });
  });
  dots.forEach(function(d){
    d.addEventListener('click', function(){ goTo(parseInt(this.dataset.index)); });
  });

  document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){
    if(e.key === 'ArrowRight' || e.key === 'ArrowDown') goTo(current + 1);
    if(e.key === 'ArrowLeft'  || e.key === 'ArrowUp')   goTo(current - 1);
  });
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
